\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When God of old came down from heaven,
\par In power and wrath He came;
\par Before His feet the clouds were riven,
\par Half darkness and half flame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. But when He came the second time,
\par He came with power and love;
\par Softer than gale at morning prime
\par Hovered His holy Dove.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The fires that rushed on Sinai down
\par In sudden torrents dread
\par Now gently light, a glorious crown
\par On every sainted head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And as on Isreal's awe-struck ear
\par The voice exceeding loud,
\par The trump that angels quake to hear,
\par Thrilled from the deep, dark cloud:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. So, when the Spirit of our God 
\par Came down His flock to find,
\par A voice from heaven was heard abroad,
\par A rushing mighty wind
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. It fills the Church of God ; it fills
\par The sinful world around ;
\par Only in stubborn hearts and wills 
\par No place for it is found.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Come, Lord; come, Wisdom, Love, and Power;
\par Open our ears to hear ;
\par Let us not miss the accepted hour;
\par Save, Lord, by love or fear.\tab 
\par                                Amen.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

